Package: @PACKAGE@
Name: @NAME@
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: iphoneos-arm
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Author: @AUTHOR@
Section: System
Priority: optional
Depends: mobilesubstrate, firmware (>= 6.0), firmware (<< 7.0)
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Description: an incoming Telegram call on the system call screen
 iOS 6 has no CallKit, and this device's SpringBoard has no SBCallAlert
 either: on 10B329 the incoming-call screen belongs to MobilePhone.app and
 is driven by a CTCall that only CommCenter can create. What SpringBoard
 does own is SBAlertItem, and its own call alert - SBCallFailureAlertItem -
 is exactly an SBAlertItem with a lock-screen slide label and two buttons.
 .
 This package adds one class of the same shape for @APPNAME@. When a call
 comes in, the app posts a Darwin notification and SpringBoard raises the
 alert: over the lock screen it becomes the standard slide bar, labelled
 with SpringBoard's own SLIDE_TO_ANSWER string, and over an app it becomes
 the standard modal alert with Decline and Answer, titled with the caller's
 name and labelled from TelephonyUI's own ANSWER and DECLINE strings.
 Sliding or tapping Answer hands the call back to the app and brings it
 forward; Decline hangs up without leaving the screen you were on.
 .
 The tweak hooks nothing. It adds a class and listens for two notifications,
 so the worst it can do to SpringBoard is nothing at all. Every selector it
 overrides is checked for existence and signature first, and if any of them
 is not the shape this build expects the class is never registered.
 Creating @PKGDIR@/disabled switches it off without uninstalling.
